  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{治|おさ}まる. The transitive pair is ⟦{治|おさ}める→治める：02462_osameru⟧ (to govern; to bring under control).\n\nUsed of pain, fever, wind, anger, or social unrest growing calm.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{治|おさ}まる: the pain subsides\n- ⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{治|おさ}まる: one's anger cools\n- ⟦{風雨|ふうう}→風雨：21731_fuuu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{治|おさ}まる: the wind and rain die down\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{収|おさ}まる→収まる：11858_osamaru⟧: to fit in; to settle — used of things fitting a space, or a situation reaching a conclusion\n- ⟦{治|なお}る→治る：19598_naoru⟧: to recover; to be cured — of an illness or injury being fully healed, not just calming",
